# Third-party Omarchy shell plugins. Installed by install.sh into
# ~/.config/omarchy/plugins/<id>/. Same contract as:
#   omarchy plugin add <url> [--enable]
# Apply clones and (with --enable) writes shell.json. It does not call the
# live omarchy-plugin-add CLI, which needs a running omarchy-shell.
#
# --enable is a seed, not a setting. It is honoured on the apply that clones
# the plugin and never again, because `omarchy plugin disable` records itself
# only as absence from shell.json and an enable on every apply would overturn
# it every update. Switch one back on with `omarchy plugin enable <id>`.
#
# Updates: monarchy-update runs `omarchy plugin update <id>` for every
# git-managed plugin with upstream changes, without --yes, so each diff is
# shown and confirmed. Plugins are unreviewed third-party code; with no
# terminal or with -y they are left as they are and listed in the summary.
#
# Deleting a row here stops nothing that is already installed. To be rid of a
# plugin: drop the row, then `omarchy plugin remove <id>`.
#
# Grok is a provider in the stock omarchy.agents panel (omarchy-agent-usage-grok).
https://github.com/crmne/omastats.git --enable
https://github.com/IM0001GT/omarchy-screens.git --enable
https://github.com/lgse/sandman.git --enable
